From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] browser: include the QButtonGroup definition

Qt's abstract-button header only forward-declares QButtonGroup. GCC 14
therefore rejects construction and member calls in toBrowserFilterSetup
because their receiver is incomplete. Include the complete Qt type where it
is used.

Patch-Source: downstream adaptation of tora 3.2 src/tools/tobrowser.cpp
Patch-License: GPL-2.0-only
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (automated upstream writes forbidden)
Applies-To: tora 3.2
Remove-When: upstream tobrowser.cpp includes QButtonGroup before using it
---
 src/tools/tobrowser.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/tools/tobrowser.cpp b/src/tools/tobrowser.cpp
--- a/src/tools/tobrowser.cpp
+++ b/src/tools/tobrowser.cpp
@@ -55,6 +55,7 @@
 #  include "core/tomysqluser.h"
 #endif
 
+#include <QButtonGroup>
 #include <QInputDialog>
 #include <QSplitter>
 #include <QToolBar>

